From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 01:21:23 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] wheel: accept riscv64 as a wheel architecture

scripts/build_wheel.sh maps `uname -m` to the manylinux platform tag
suffix and fails the build for anything but x86_64/aarch64, and
mooncake-wheel/setup.py's get_arch() raises ValueError on the same
condition. Nothing else in the CPU build is architecture-specific: the
PAUSE() macros already have a generic fallback and the Go c-shared
etcd wrapper builds for linux/riscv64.

Map riscv64 to itself in both places so the non-CUDA wheel builds on
riscv64 the same way it does on x86_64 and aarch64.

Upstream-Status: To upstream [not submitted from this automated port run; needs a pull request against kvcache-ai/Mooncake]
---
 mooncake-wheel/setup.py | 2 ++
 scripts/build_wheel.sh  | 3 +++
 2 files changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/mooncake-wheel/setup.py b/mooncake-wheel/setup.py
index 56cb1c5..20bd7aa 100644
--- a/mooncake-wheel/setup.py
+++ b/mooncake-wheel/setup.py
@@ -117,6 +117,8 @@ def get_arch() -> str:
             return "x86_64"
         if platform.machine() in ("arm64", "aarch64"):
             return "aarch64"
+        if platform.machine() == "riscv64":
+            return "riscv64"
     elif sys.platform == "darwin":
         # Return only the arch; macOS deployment target lives in get_system()
         return "aarch64" if platform.machine() in ("arm64", "aarch64") else "x86_64"
diff --git a/scripts/build_wheel.sh b/scripts/build_wheel.sh
index eed2576..ebb0a67 100755
--- a/scripts/build_wheel.sh
+++ b/scripts/build_wheel.sh
@@ -400,6 +400,9 @@ case "$ARCH" in
     x86_64)
         ARCH_SUFFIX="x86_64"
         ;;
+    riscv64)
+        ARCH_SUFFIX="riscv64"
+        ;;
     *)
         echo "Error: Unknown or unsupported architecture $ARCH. Failing the build."
         exit 1
